{"abstract":"Participatory Design (PD) aims for inclusivity, but the level of inclusion varies widely. Inclusion often means integrating stakeholder perspectives into design processes, often neglecting bi-directionality, where communities also have agendas. True collaboration rests on mutual understanding, acknowledging the dynamic nature of community collaboration and the holistic impact of shaping relationships. This workshop will explore collaboration challenges and practices with marginalized communities. It will draw on the organisers’ extensive experiences with diverse groups, including nomadic and resettled indigenous communities in Namibia, Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh, and Syrian war refugees in Jordan. The workshop encourages sharing and reflecting on experiences with marginalized communities, welcoming contributions from participants to enrich discussions and enhance collective understanding of collaborative practices.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rodil, Kasper","Kandjengo, Shorty","Maasz, Donovan","Ahsan, Hasib","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776407"],"event":{"acronym":"PDC","title":"Participatory Design Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Namibia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Donkerbos Community","Namibia University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Global South","Marginalised Communities","Participatory Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparative insights for community based co design bi directional inclusive strategies between marginalised communities and researchers in participatory design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85204902234","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776407","identifier":[{"id":"85204902234","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-663e67b2-4ac5-41f4-b969-439ccdfeb60d"],"keyword":["Global South","Marginalised Communities","Participatory Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-769FFC5266B6C071E7C61CF385DE0167"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"na","key":"donkerbos community","loc":["Namibia","Africa"],"name":"Donkerbos Community","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"na","key":"namibia university of science and technology","loc":["Namibia","Africa"],"name":"Namibia University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"rodilpau","last":"Rodil","name":"Rodil, Kasper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shorty","key":"kandjengopau","last":"Kandjengo","name":"Kandjengo, Shorty","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Donovan","key":"maaszpau","last":"Maasz","name":"Maasz, Donovan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3661455.3669894","isbn":["9798400706547"],"pages":"207-210","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"PDC '24: Proceedings of the Participatory Design Conference 2024: Exploratory Papers and Workshops - Volume 2","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204902234"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-663e67b2-4ac5-41f4-b969-439ccdfeb60d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Comparative Insights for Community-Based Co-design: Bi-directional Inclusive Strategies Between Marginalised Communities and Researchers in Participatory Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776407","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Participatory Design (PD) aims for inclusivity, but the level of inclusion varies widely. Inclusion often means integrating stakeholder perspectives into design processes, often neglecting bi-directionality, where communities also have agendas. True collaboration rests on mutual understanding, acknowledging the dynamic nature of community collaboration and the holistic impact of shaping relationships. This workshop will explore collaboration challenges and practices with marginalized communities. It will draw on the organisers’ extensive experiences with diverse groups, including nomadic and resettled indigenous communities in Namibia, Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh, and Syrian war refugees in Jordan. The workshop encourages sharing and reflecting on experiences with marginalized communities, welcoming contributions from participants to enrich discussions and enhance collective understanding of collaborative practices.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Rodil, Kasper","Kandjengo, Shorty","Maasz, Donovan","Ahsan, Hasib","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-736429"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-16","place":"Sibu, my","start":"2024-08-12","title":"18th Participatory Design Conference","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Namibia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Donkerbos Community","Namibia University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Community based co design","Marginalised Communities","Participatory Design","Workshop"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparative insights for community based co design bi directional inclusive strategies between marginalised communities and researchers in participatory design","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85204902234&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-736429","identifier":[{"id":"85204902234","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-dbfd54b5-466f-4f3c-8768-7a62d27384c7"],"keyword":["Community-based co-design","Participatory Design","Workshop","marginalised communities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-769FFC5266B6C071E7C61CF385DE0167"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Human Machine Interaction","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Centre for Sustainable and Digital Transformation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"na","key":"donkerbos community","loc":["Namibia","Africa"],"name":"Donkerbos Community","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"na","key":"namibia university of science and technology","loc":["Namibia","Africa"],"name":"Namibia University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"rodilpau","last":"Rodil","locid":"43295420-1fb5-48c4-b8cb-e6fb3c72503f","name":"Rodil, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-6737-7342","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shorty","key":"kandjengopau","last":"Kandjengo","name":"Kandjengo, Shorty","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Donovan","key":"maaszpau","last":"Maasz","name":"Maasz, Donovan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vincenzo","key":"dandreapedh","last":"D'Andrea","name":"D'Andrea, Vincenzo","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rogerio Abreu","key":"depaulapedh","last":"de Paula","name":"de Paula, Rogerio Abreu","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kasper","key":"rodilpedh","last":"Rodil","name":"Rodil, Kasper","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"lamaspedh","last":"Lamas","name":"Lamas, David","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Naska","key":"goagosespedh","last":"Goagoses","name":"Goagoses, Naska","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Asnath Paula","key":"kambungapedh","last":"Kambunga","name":"Kambunga, Asnath Paula","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"tanyongwenpedh","last":"Tan Yong Wen","name":"Tan Yong Wen, Daniel","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Chiara","key":"delgaudiopedh","last":"Del Gaudio","name":"Del Gaudio, Chiara","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mika Yasuoka","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Mika Yasuoka","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Heike","key":"winschierstheophiluspedh","last":"Winschiers-Theophilus","name":"Winschiers-Theophilus, Heike","rank":15,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tariq","key":"zamanpedh","last":"Zaman","name":"Zaman, Tariq","rank":16,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3661455.3669894","eisbn":["9798400706547"],"pages":"207-210","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 18th Participatory Design Conference","title":"PDC '24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204902234"],"sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","17. Partnerships for the Goals","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dbfd54b5-466f-4f3c-8768-7a62d27384c7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Comparative Insights for Community-Based Co-design : Bi-directional Inclusive Strategies Between Marginalised Communities and Researchers in Participatory Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-736429","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The mental health issues of refugees displaced by violence and affected by humanitarian crises are significant but may be underestimated by healthcare providers. This paper reports on a five-month field trial of a digital screening tool in the Kutupalong refugee camp in Bangladesh. The screening tool is based on the WHO SRQ-20 standard with twenty questions to identify people showing symptoms of mental health issues. The paper demonstrates that not only can digital mental health interventions identify people with symptoms of mental health issues in a refugee camp, but the approach can also identify predictors of mental health issues. First, findings show that of 1630 persons screened, 20.1% exhibited indications of significant mental health issues. Second, a binary logistic regression analysis finds that three of the questions or variables have high ‘odds ratios’ and are, therefore, significant in their ability to predict mental health issues. These predictors are substantiated through semi-structured interviews with the refugees that highlight particular issues of concern.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ahsan, Hasib","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776401"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital health","Digital mental health interventions","HCI4D","ICT4D","Public health"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital mental health in humanitarian crisis in bangladesh","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106869518/Digital_Mental_Health_in_Humanitarian_Crisis_in_Bangladesh.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study received funding from the Novo Nordisk Foundation[grant numbers 0055633 & 0062495]"],"id":"S01-000.00-776401","identifier":[{"id":"85201014459","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5a6d3228-5d5d-4e76-9c07-e055d7709304"],"keyword":["Binary logistic regression","Digital Health","Digital mental health interventions","HCI4D","ICT4D","Public health","Rohingya Refugee"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-63F1BF988636F7FACFEDCADBC3EC78CE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106869518/Digital_Mental_Health_in_Humanitarian_Crisis_in_Bangladesh.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-66982-8_20","eisbn":["9783031669828"],"isbn":["9783031669811"],"issn":["18684238"],"pages":"286-302","publisher":"Springer","series":"IFIP Advances in Information and Communication Technology","status":"p","title":"Implications of Information and Digital Technologies for Development","volume":"708"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201014459"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5a6d3228-5d5d-4e76-9c07-e055d7709304"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digital Mental Health in Humanitarian Crisis in Bangladesh","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776401","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper delves into the emotional landscape of researchers engaged in participatory design and action research. It addresses the less-discussed aspects of unwanted emotions, such as guilt and shame, experienced by researchers during and post-project. The paper explores the guilty dichotomy between the researchers' intent to contribute positively and the reality of unmet expectations. The unease stemming from perceived exploitation and the limitations of project impact is scrutinised, highlighting the tightrope walked in participatory design. Furthermore, the paper discusses the paradox of professional recognition versus the ongoing adversities faced by what may be marginalised communities. Through reflective analysis, this paper contributes to a deeper understanding of the emotional landscape traversed by researchers in participatory design and action research. It underscores the need for supportive frameworks that address these emotional aspects, advocating for ethical reflexivity and sustained engagement strategies that align closely with community needs and well-being.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Ahsan, Hasib"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776417"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital mental health interventions","ICT4D action research design research","ICT4D participative development participatory design","Participatory Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the researcher s plight guilt and shame in participatory design and action research","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3661455.3669865","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776417","identifier":[{"id":"85204888908","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7a44eac9-4787-422b-bef1-e5b587e7d83d"],"keyword":["ICT4D, action research, design research","ICT4D, participative development, participatory design","Participatory Design","digital mental health interventions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2BA9A10BF206810F51B44AADA18D7991"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3661455.3669865","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3661455.3669865","eisbn":["9798400706547"],"pages":"19-23","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"PDC '24: Proceedings of the Participatory Design Conference 2024: Exploratory Papers and Workshops - Volume 2","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204888908"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7a44eac9-4787-422b-bef1-e5b587e7d83d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Researcher's Plight: Guilt and Shame in Participatory Design and Action Research","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776417","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Drawing on ethnographic fieldwork in a refugee camp in Jordan, this article investigates how datafication through digital screening technologies helps shape mental health issues in the face of widespread uneasiness about the subject, especially among the intended beneficiaries. We argue that the refugees and their health care providers face a dilemma: on the one hand, the desire to make mental health issues visible and clinically actionable through datafication and, on the other hand, the wish to keep mental health issues out of public view to avoid potential stigma.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Ahsan, Hasib"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712531"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data","Datafication","Global Health","Mental health","Refugees","Stigma"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the trouble of stigma in the age of datafication screening for mental health issues in a refugee camp in jordan","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85169923049","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation [grant no. NNF21SH0069701]"],"id":"S01-000.00-712531","identifier":[{"id":"85169923049","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7ca80feb-c418-4539-af15-2546d769cb30"],"keyword":["Data","Datafication","Global Health","Mental Health","Refugees","Stigma"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0E38576BBF35EC6E076DFEAFA949B14D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/01459740.2023.2250060","issn":["01459740","15455882"],"issue":"7","journal":"Medical Anthropology: Cross Cultural Studies in Health and Illness","pages":"623-636","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Medical Anthropology: Cross Cultural Studies in Health and Illness","title_org":"Medical Anthropology: Cross-Cultural Studies in Health and Illness","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85169923049"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7ca80feb-c418-4539-af15-2546d769cb30"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Trouble of Stigma in the Age of Datafication: Screening for Mental Health Issues in a Refugee Camp in Jordan","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712531","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Based on fieldwork in five distinct projects, this thesis investigates the role of human infrastructure in the context of digital interventions in the Global South. The settings are an agriculture voice message service for smallholder farmers in Bangladesh, an agricultural information service using phone text messages (SMS) also for farmers in Bangladesh, a for-profit service for farmers in Cambodia using digital applications, a digital mental health intervention for Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh and a study of the reordering of everyday life through digital technologies in Bangladesh during the Covid-19 pandemic. The focus on human infrastructure is inspired by research within Information & Communication Technologies and Development (ICTD), Computer-Supported Cooperative Work (CSCW), Human-Computer Interaction (HCI), Science Technology Studies (STS) and more. My findings contribute to research and practice by nuancing our understanding of the role of human infrastructure in digital interventions in the Global South. That is, I empirically and conceptually extend the discussion by pointing out how human infrastructure may be 'configured,' 'trained' and 'unravelled' in the context of digital interventions in the Global South. I show how one cannot take the human infrastructure for granted in the sense that it has to be both configured and trained and hence is not simply somehow there. Further, I discuss how a human infrastructure may unravel in the context of digital interventions in the global South and the consequences this may have for continued service provision. These contributions may be useful for both researchers and practitioners as it adds to our understanding of the key role of human infrastructure in digital interventions in the Global South and elsewhere.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Ahsan, Hasib"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718906"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of human infrastructure investigating digital interventions in the global south","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109068292/PhD_Thesis_Final_Version_Hasib_Ahsan.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718906","ids":["itu-af65277d-47a2-4881-84e1-e36103e362fb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CF2F9E20724B6E9F65527FF1A5168F04"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109068292/PhD_Thesis_Final_Version_Hasib_Ahsan.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788779494015"],"issn":["16023536"],"issue":"205","pages":"134","series":"ITU-DS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-af65277d-47a2-4881-84e1-e36103e362fb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Role of Human Infrastructure : Investigating Digital Interventions in the Global South","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718906","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper offers an exploration of everyday life during the Covid-19 pandemic in Bangladesh with a focus on how it has been reordered through commonplace digital technologies and services. We present findings from a qualitative field study. Themes emerging from the findings suggest that digital technologies have been important to the reordering of everyday life during the pandemic: videoconferencing have been instrumental in allowing urban residents to work from home, digital money has enabled workers in rural areas to continue financial transactions, and social media has been a source of news and rumours during the pandemic. However, the benefits of the digital reordering of everyday life are unevenly distributed. The themes emerging are used to frame a discussion of the notion of reordering compared to the concept of resilience within ICTD.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ahsan, Hasib","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695239"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["COVID 19 pandemic","Digital technologies","Everyday life","Qualitative field study","Reordering and resilience in ICTD"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the reordering of everyday life through digital technologies during the covid 000000000019 pandemic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3572334.3572375","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695239","identifier":[{"id":"85159702798","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-43c93d75-4474-4d4f-a9eb-296e477ef4b4"],"keyword":["Covid-19 pandemic","Digital technologies","Everyday life","Qualitative field study","Reordering and resilience in ICTD"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-66FFD637F2EA28B265397486A09ABCE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3572334.3572375","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3572334.3572375","pages":"1-7","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ICTD 2022: ACM Conference on The International Conference on Information &amp; Communication Technologies and Development (ICTD)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159702798"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-43c93d75-4474-4d4f-a9eb-296e477ef4b4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Reordering of Everyday Life through Digital technologies During the Covid-19 Pandemic","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695239","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Screening refugees for mental health issues, medical assistants use a digital tool that produces a numerical score but also, importantly, attunes to the moods of their clients and the atmospheres of their homes. In this article, we propose the concept of numeration-attunement as helpful for medical anthropology. Drawing on ethnographic fieldwork conducted among med-ical assistants working in the Kutapalong refugee camp in Bangladesh, we explore their assessment of the mental health of the refugees: its numeration- attunement. To develop the notion of numeration-attunement, we draw on numeration research as well as phenomenology. Comprehending how med-ical assistants assess the mental health of refugees requires attention both to numeration and datafication by way of a screening tool as well as the revelatory character of attunement to moods.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Ahsan, Hasib"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384901"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bangladesh","Datafication","Mental health","Moods","Numerations","Refugee","Rohingya"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"of numbers and moods screening for mental health issues in a rohingya refugee camp in bangladesh","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01459740.2022.2113396","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384901","identifier":[{"id":"85137819849","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f678ca8c-f19a-4c37-a635-81adb8cd098d"],"keyword":["Bangladesh","Datafication","Mental health","Moods","Numerations","Refugee","Rohingya"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-291F023CAB25CD80CB8AAC38A1B934C4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/epdf/10.1080/01459740.2022.2113396?needAccess=true&role=button","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01459740.2022.2113396","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/01459740.2022.2113396","issn":["01459740","15455882"],"issue":"8","journal":"Medical Anthropology: Cross Cultural Studies in Health and Illness","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Medical Anthropology: Cross Cultural Studies in Health and Illness","title_org":"Medical Anthropology: Cross-Cultural Studies in Health and Illness","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137819849"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f678ca8c-f19a-4c37-a635-81adb8cd098d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Of Numbers and Moods: Screening for Mental Health Issues in a Rohingya Refugee Camp in Bangladesh","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384901","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Based on a field study, this paper presents an analysis of the ICT-driven agricultural initiative in Cambodia and shows how it may be understood as infrastructuring for value chain, for microcredit, and for capacity building. The paper considers the relational, connected, emerging, and intentional character of the initiative. In doing so, it outlines an approach to the investigation and conception of infrastructuring for smallholder farming in the Global South.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ahsan, Hasib","Christensen, Lars Rune","Kitura, K"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382109"],"event":{"acronym":"C&T","title":"International Conference on Communities and Technologies"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["Hong Kong"],"glorg":["Agribuddy Ltd.","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["Capacity building","Global South farming","ICT driven agriculture","Infrastructuring","Value chain"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"agribuddy infrastructuring for smallholder farming in cambodia","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3461564.3461576","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382109","identifier":[{"id":"85109407557","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3918fa3b-a409-4469-ba34-27ae15a6dc5e"],"keyword":["Capacity building","Global South farming","ICT-driven agriculture","Infrastructuring","Value chain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EDD5230F3B4778175A51FE6852EA4449"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3461564.3461576","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"hk","key":"agribuddy ltd","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"Agribuddy Ltd.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"K","key":"kiturapau","last":"Kitura","name":"Kitura, K","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3461564.3461576","pages":"309","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 10th International Conference on Communities &amp; Technologies: Wicked Problems in the Age Of Tech"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85109407557"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3918fa3b-a409-4469-ba34-27ae15a6dc5e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Agribuddy: Infrastructuring for Smallholder Farming in Cambodia","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382109","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The COVID-19 “infodemic” has resulted in the widespread dissemination of counterfeit medical advice, hoaxes, fake products, and phoney information about the virus and responses. As a result, computational methods for determining any information’s authenticity to improve trust in public health awareness and policy decisions are profoundly discussed in the scientific community. Even before the pandemic, mis- and disinformation, including fake news, have been observed in the online world in significant numbers for numerous business, political and personal reasons. Moreover, many of these fake news was published from sources believed to be reliable. In contrast, some other fake news was fabricated in a way that would be easily trusted and shared by the general people in social media. COVID-19 related fake news has enormous effects on both the offline and online community, and thus, it challenges government initiatives for proper health intervention. Therefore, interest in research in this area has risen to understand the problem both socially and technically. In this paper, we attempt to understand how we can help student Internet users of colleges from the lower-middle-income country, Bangladesh, in Southeast Asia, to distinguish COVID-19 misinformation. Our study reveals that providing related news as supplementary information to any online news helps students make better decision about news authenticity. Statistical analyses on the survey data show that male students were found to be more accurate than female students to detect mis- and disinformation; students from the urban areas could detect misleading news better than students from villages; and that students from Science background demonstrated overall best performance, while students from Madrasah background, who are all male, could not produce a significant improvement. We conclude that the female students in general and male students of Madrasah, who spend the least amount of time online among all the student Internet users, are the most vulnerable groups to fake news.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Uddin, Borhan","Reza, Nahid","Islam, Md Saiful","Ahsan, Hasib","Amin, Mohammad Ruhul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382790"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","OECD"],"country":["Bangladesh","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fordham University","Shahjalal University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["COVID 19 Fake News","Identification of Fake News","Mis and Disinformation in Bangladesh"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fighting against fake news during pandemic era does providing related news help student internet users to detect covid 000000000019 misinformation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3447535.3462508","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382790","identifier":[{"id":"85109026341","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-658f3c55-b4c1-4140-aa75-100e88309388"],"keyword":["COVID-19 Fake News","Identification of Fake News","Mis- and Disinformation in Bangladesh"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-147A5DB7EAD9768816D5116833CB9978"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3447535.3462508","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"bd","key":"shahjalal university of science and technology","loc":["Bangladesh","Asia, South"],"name":"Shahjalal University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"fordham university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Fordham University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Borhan","key":"uddinpau","last":"Uddin","name":"Uddin, Borhan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nahid","key":"rezapau","last":"Reza","name":"Reza, Nahid","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Md Saiful","key":"islampau","last":"Islam","name":"Islam, Md Saiful","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad Ruhul","key":"aminpau","last":"Amin","name":"Amin, Mohammad Ruhul","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3447535.3462508","eisbn":["9781450383301"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"WebSci 2021: 13th ACM Web Science Conference 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85109026341"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-658f3c55-b4c1-4140-aa75-100e88309388"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fighting Against Fake News During Pandemic Era: Does Providing Related News Help Student Internet Users to Detect COVID-19 Misinformation?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382790","year":"2021","yearsub":"202